From 5e57e985fedfd0ee61a03f13eef33af76a7e86f0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bogdan Codres <bogdan.codres@windriver.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 19:45:21 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] kdump-tools: blacklist idxd in the kdump kernel

On Sapphire Rapids and Granite Rapids D systems where the Intel DSA
device has been configured (e.g. through the Intel Device Plugins
application), the idxd driver fails to probe in the kdump kernel
because the device is HALTED when booted with reset_devices:

  idxd 0000:f6:01.0: Device is HALTED!
  idxd 0000:f6:01.0: Intel(R) IDXD DMA Engine init failed
  ida_free called for id=0 which is not allocated.

The error path in idxd_pci_probe() frees the idxd object twice, which
corrupts the slab. The kdump kernel then oopses (e.g. in ___slab_alloc
from systemd-udevd or kacpid) and, since it runs with nr_cpus=1, hangs
in RCU stalls. kdump-tools-dump.service never runs, so no vmcore or
dmesg is saved and the node needs a hard reset.

The kdump kernel does not need DSA, so add idxd and idxd_bus to the
module_blacklist= list, as is already done for other drivers that are
not needed to save a vmcore.

Important: this should be seen as a workaround. The final patch will
be in kernel. However, the upstream patch is not yet finalized. The
discussion are on-going here:
https://lore.kernel.org/all/20261012-wt-idxd-fixes-v1-0-30a35a445077@intel.com/

Signed-off-by: Bogdan Codres <bogdan.codres@windriver.com>
---
 debian/rules | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/debian/rules b/debian/rules
index 1db33eb..b631885 100755
--- a/debian/rules
+++ b/debian/rules
@@ -15,7 +15,7 @@ else ifeq ($(DEB_HOST_ARCH),ppc64el)
 	KDUMP_CMDLINE_APPEND += maxcpus=1 irqpoll noirqdistrib usbcore.nousb
 else
 	KDUMP_CMDLINE_APPEND += nr_cpus=1 irqpoll usbcore.nousb pci=noaer
-	KDUMP_CMDLINE_APPEND += module_blacklist=ice,i40e,iavf,bnxt_en,bnxt_re,ib_core,mlx5_core,mlx5_ib,mlx_compat,vfio,oct_ep_phc,e1000e,ixgbe,ixgbevf,drbd,tg3,igb
+	KDUMP_CMDLINE_APPEND += module_blacklist=ice,i40e,iavf,bnxt_en,bnxt_re,ib_core,mlx5_core,mlx5_ib,mlx_compat,vfio,oct_ep_phc,e1000e,ixgbe,ixgbevf,drbd,tg3,igb,idxd,idxd_bus
 	KDUMP_CMDLINE_APPEND += cgroup_disable=memory transparent_hugepage=never systemd.mask=systemd-sysctl.service systemd.mask=networking.service
 	KDUMP_CMDLINE_APPEND += systemd.mask=iscsid.service udev.children_max=2
 endif
